-- title:
--   Igusa components of the descended two-chart model, q=2
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=2$, let $M'$ be a nonzero level with $q\nmid M'$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a nonunit of $A$. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ consisting exactly of the supersingular places (those places that are rational, satisfy `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and whose value at `jGeomGen` lies in `ssJSet q`). Assume `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` $\le$ `fieldBar q M'`, and let $R_0$ be a `ConstantReduction` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $A$ with residue field `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` whose residue map is computed coefficientwise on Laurent series with coefficients in $A$. Let $\pi\in A$ satisfy $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$, let $\zeta$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and let $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}:\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)\to$ valuation subrings of `fieldBar q M'` and $O_{\mathrm{SS}}:W\to$ valuation subrings of `fieldBar q M'` be families subject to: $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ at $\ell=[1:0]$ consists of the quotients $x/y$ of Laurent series with coefficients in $A$ whose denominator has nonzero coefficientwise reduction; every $\ell$ is reached from $[1:0]$ by some $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ through `redQ q`, with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}\,\ell$ the pullback of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}[1:0]$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ is injective; and the $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}\,\ell$ are permuted by pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for all $\zeta'$ and $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}\,s$ meets $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in $A$, is fixed by all these pullbacks, contains an element $t$ with $t-a$ a unit for every $a\in A$, and contains the image of every $f$ in the integers of $R_0$ that is regular wherever $\hat\jmath$ is (the image of `jq` under `coeffEmb`) and whose $R_0$-residue lies at $s$, with $f$ congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}\,s$ to any $a\in A$ whose residue is the value of that $R_0$-residue at $s$. Descent data: a subfield $K_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q}/K_0$ algebraic and $\pi\in K_0$; a henselian discrete valuation domain $A_0$ with an injective local ring map $\iota:A_0\to A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is $A\cap K_0$ and which induces a surjection onto $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$; a uniformiser $\varpi_0$ of $A_0$ with $\iota\varpi_0=\pi$; the subfield $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'` of those elements all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in $K_0$, which contains $\hat\jmath$ and is an $A_0$-algebra via $\iota$, with $\hat\jmath\neq0$ in $F_0$; and $S\subseteq F_0$ equal to $\{\hat\jmath\}$ or to $\{\hat\jmath^{-1}\}$. Then there is a family $\mathfrak q:\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)\to$ ideals of `TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlg A₀ F₀ S`, the subalgebra of elements of $F_0$ integral over $A_0[S]$, such that for each $\ell$ and each $x\in F_0$ one has $x\in O_{\mathrm{Ig}}\,\ell$ if and only if $x=b/c$ with $b,c$ in that chart algebra and $c\notin\mathfrak q\,\ell$; each $\mathfrak q\,\ell$ is a minimal prime over the ideal generated by the image of the maximal ideal of $A_0$; $\mathfrak q$ is injective; and every minimal prime over that ideal equals some $\mathfrak q\,\ell$.
--
--   This identifies the components of the special fibre of either chart of the two-chart integral model of the descended field $F_0$ over $A_0$ with the $q+1$ points of $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$, the localisation at the component indexed by $\ell$ being the Igusa valuation ring $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}\,\ell$ intersected with $F_0$; it is the $q=2$ case, the prime $q$ being assumed equal to $2$ throughout. It is used by the subsequent statements describing the maximal ideals of the chart algebras attached to the Igusa and Drinfeld valuation rings on the descended model.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_exists_primes_chartAlg_localization_eq_igusaRing_minimal_injective_descent_of_eq_two.lean

